```javascript
function packEntities(entities) {
  const buffer = new Uint16Array(Math.ceil(entities.length / 2));

  let offset = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < entities.length; i++) {
    const entity = entities[i];
    const id = entity.id;
    const size = entity.size;

    // Pack id (4 bits) and size (3 bits) into a single 16-bit value
    const packed = (id << 3) | size;
    buffer[offset] = packed;

    // Move to the next 16-bit position
    offset += 1;
  }

  return buffer.buffer;
}

function unpackEntities(buffer, length) {
  const entities = [];
  let offset = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < length; i += 2) {
    const packed = new Uint16Array(buffer, i, 1)[0];

    // Extract id (4 bits) and size (3 bits) from the packed value
    const id = packed >> 3;
    const size = packed & 7;

    entities.push({ id, size });

    // Move to the next 16-bit position
    offset += 2;
  }

  return entities;
}
```

In the `packEntities` function, we create a Uint16Array buffer and pack the entities into it using bitwise operations. The id and size are combined into a single 16-bit value, and each pair of entities is stored in a single 16-bit value.

In the `unpackEntities` function, we extract the id and size from each packed value and create an array of entities. The id is extracted by shifting the packed value 3 bits to the right, and the size is extracted by performing a bitwise AND operation with 7 (since the size can only be 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6).

